  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Information Systems phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this investment in health information systems is to help countries in the Indo-Pacific region to mobilise quality, inclusive and equitable health data to ensure healthy lives and promote wellbeing, and reduce inequalities within and among countries (SDG 3 and SDG 10). Strong health information systems and data for decision making are central to making best use of limited resources to improve individual and population health.

This program is DFAT&#x2019;s second phase of investment in this area, and builds on the momentum of earlier programs with an increased emphasis on ensuring that health information systems are supported sustainably from within the region, that data standards and interoperability are key considerations, that digital health strategies are in place, and that countries are able to harness the data for decision-making.</narrative>
  </description>
